    "created_at": "2025-07-02T02:23:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-02T02:23:10Z",
    "body": "It could also be useful to describe the interaction of a canvas' own tone mapping with [`dynamic-range-limit`](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-hdr/#the-dynamic-range-limit-property), and other external influences, like the browser or OS wanting to constrain HDR to match ambient conditions and/or reduce battery usage.\n\nMaybe it could be as simple as saying that the latter two \"just\" reduce the available headroom?\nOr should `dynamic-range-limit` be accompanied by its own tone mapping parameters to be applied to any element, and to replace or somehow be combined with the canvas'?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
