    "created_at": "2025-07-02T07:42:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-02T07:43:07Z",
    "body": "Good point. I added a section clarifying the interactions.\n\nThe `dynamic-range-limit` behaves the same for all elements (canvas, image, video, etc), namely, it limits the HDR headroom used for display.\n\nIn the specific case of `\"extended\"`, lowering the `dynamic-range-limit` will result in the browser clamping(*) the canvas to a lower HDR headroom. Because the tone mapping is trivial for `\"extended\"`, it happens to be the case that lowering to `dynamic-range-limit:standard` will happen to be the same as setting `mode:\"standard\"`.\n\nOf note is that the goal in [this section](https://github.com/ccameron-chromium/ColorWeb-CG/blob/master/canvas2d_tone_map.md#nontrivial-tone-mapping-modes) is that once we have finished standardization, it will be possible to author a video, canvas, and image, that will render the same on all displays, and also at all values of `dynamic-range-limit`.\n\n(*) not necessary per-component clamping, but projecting to the target gamut, ideally preserving hue",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
